# rfc-011-category-enhancements.mdc

## Title
RFC 011 – Category Enhancements & Organizational Improvements

## Summary
This RFC introduces improvements to the category system for better video organization, user navigation, and admin control. Enhancements include custom ordering, category-level metadata, and carousel management.

---

## Goals
- Allow custom ordering of categories and their displayed videos
- Add descriptive metadata and links to each category
- Manage homepage carousel display for each category

## Database Extensions
### `categories` Table
Add fields:
- `order_index` (int, nullable): Custom display order
- `description` (text, nullable): Rich category explanation
- `topic_link` (text, nullable): External resource URL (e.g. Wikipedia, Docs)
- `helpful_links` (jsonb, nullable): Additional useful links
- `show_in_carousel` (boolean, default false): Whether to show on homepage slider
- `carousel_order` (int, nullable): Ordering on homepage carousel

### `videos` Table
- `category_order_index` (int, nullable): Ordering of videos within a category

## UI Enhancements
- Admin panel form for managing:
  - Category description and topic link
  - Helpful links (as an array or tag input)
  - Enable/disable homepage carousel display
  - Drag-and-drop sorting UI for carousel order

## Permissions
| Role        | Category Management        |
|-------------|----------------------------|
| Admin       | ✅ Full create/edit/delete |
| Team Lead   | 🟡 View and suggest only   |
| User        | ❌ No access               |

## Timeline
**Sprint 11**
- Update database schema with new fields
- Build UI form and inputs in Admin dashboard
- Implement drag-and-drop sorting for carousel
- Integrate fields into video/category creation workflows

